# [INPUT]: Git line-ending and whitespace matching for repository sources and exact-byte artifacts.
# [OUTPUT]: LF source checkouts and unchanged license, notice and internal acceptance bytes.
# [POS]: Root checkout policy; artifact formatting does not change source whitespace checks.
# [PROTOCOL]: Update this header when making changes, then check README.md.

# Line endings are not a local preference here. Builds, the public audit and packaged
# verification compare these trees byte for byte, and the release manifest pins their
# digests, so every checkout must produce the same bytes on every platform. Nothing in
# the tree is a Windows script, so LF everywhere costs nothing.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Redistributed upstream license text and generated supply-chain notices are artifacts,
# not source: their exact bytes are the identity being asserted. Never convert them.
LICENSE -text
NOTICE.txt -text
*.NOTICE.txt -text
OFL.txt -text


# Unified-diff context lines and native logs retain their original spaces and bytes.
DEV/chat/artifact-design/adaptation.patch -text whitespace=-blank-at-eol
DEV/chat/artifact-design/evidence/**/*.log -text whitespace=-blank-at-eol

